==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-get rid of.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|get<,,got,got[UK]:gotten[US]> rid of}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|idiom}} To [[rid]] oneself of; to [[discard]]; to [[remove]]; to [[abolish]]; to [[lose]].
#: {{syn|en|dismiss|drop|lose|shed|Thesaurus:junk}}
#: ''Over the weekend he spent some time '''getting rid of''' the clothes he no longer wears.''
#: ''I want to '''get rid of''' your influence over my life!''
#* '''March 23, 1727''', {{w|Alexander Pope}}, letter to {{w|Jonathan Swift}}
#*: to '''get rid of''' fools and scoundrels

====Usage notes====
One is said to ''get rid of'' something unwanted or undesirable. The term is not neutral; it implies that one's situation is improved by ''getting rid of'' that thing. 

The term belongs to a less formal register than the verbs given in the definition.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|be rid of}}

